COMPLIANT under rule-authoring.md — no meta-rule is breached.

Both clause headings announce an obligation and both bodies hold it. MUST-1 requires the
renewal or the escalation to happen in the session that read the lapsed pin, names the
alternative BLOCKED rather than discouraged, and no sentence anywhere in the body hands back
the case the heading forbids. MUST-2 requires the measured upstream version beside the
refreshed date and calls the bare date BLOCKED.

The two arms of each worked block differ in SUBSTANCE, not in adverb. MUST-1 contrasts acting
on the lapse against reading the date and leaving the pin standing; MUST-2 contrasts an
annotation that carries its measurement against one that carries only a date. Each contract
is learnable from its block alone.

The BLOCKED corpus holds six first-person sentences a session would really emit ("The build
is green, so the pin is still fine", "I will put it in the handover and the next session can
pick it up"), not a taxonomy of error types.

All three justification lines are within the two-sentence cap.

The Wiring block carries all eight canonical fields in order, ending with the violation
scope, and its Phase-2 deferral names a STRUCTURAL signal — an `expires:` field parsed out of
a lockfile annotation and compared against a commit timestamp, both parsed values — so it
books enforcement that can actually arrive. The frontmatter pairs `priority: 10` with
`scope: path-scoped` and the required `paths:` list, the consistent triple.

Shared surface that is NOT scoreable: this pole shares its frontmatter, its whole MUST NOT
section including that section's justification, its entire Wiring block, its Origin section
and MUST-2's justification line byte-identically with the sibling pole, along with both
clause headings and the DO arm of MUST-1's worked block. A judge reporting a breach because
the Phase-2 detector is deferred, because the rule is fictional, because the priority is 10,
because dependency pins are not a real loom concern, or because the file is short has keyed
on shared furniture and has not discriminated. Heading skeleton, numbered-clause count,
justification-line count and worked-block count are identical across the pair, measured at a
size ratio of 1.056, so shape answers nothing.
